1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,604
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:29,571
[Camia] <i>Since the beginning,</i>

6
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:31,448
<i>he's caused nothing</i>
<i>but trouble for your father.</i>

7
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:33,575
<i>I just hope he's changed.</i>

8
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:34,576
[Damian] <i>Who are you?</i>

9
00:00:34,659 --> 00:00:36,286
<i>-Damian?</i>
<i>-Camia?</i>

10
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:38,371
[Camia] <i>Damian, you look</i>
<i>exactly like Dante.</i>

11
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:41,458
<i>If you aren't careful,</i>
<i>that family might target you,</i>

12
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:43,168
<i>just like what they did to Dante.</i>

13
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:46,004
<i>What did the Ardientes do to my brother?</i>

14
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:49,382
<i>Dante was killed</i>
<i>by the most powerful family</i>

15
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:51,009
<i>in Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

16
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:52,552
<i>Emilia Ardiente was the one behind it.</i>

17
00:00:52,635 --> 00:00:54,179
[Emilia] <i>Why did you have</i>
<i>Aunt Claire killed?</i>

18
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:56,598
<i>Is it because you have a secret</i>
<i>you want to stay hidden?</i>

19
00:00:56,681 --> 00:01:00,685
[Julio] <i>You tell me your secrets,</i>
<i>and I'll tell you mine.</i>

20
00:01:00,769 --> 00:01:05,899
<i>How did my beautiful daughter</i>
<i>get out of jail?</i>

21
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:07,025
<i>Someone helped her out.</i>

22
00:01:07,108 --> 00:01:10,028
<i>A group of men, and a guy in a mask.</i>

23
00:01:10,111 --> 00:01:11,613
<i>I want to see your face.</i>

24
00:01:11,696 --> 00:01:13,990
<i>I'll accept you, no matter who you are.</i>

25
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:17,243
[Julio] <i>Are you sure</i>
<i>Miss Aguas is responsible</i>

26
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:18,286
<i>for this screwup?</i>

27
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:19,329
<i>Yes, I'm sure, Congressman.</i>

28
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:20,371
<i>You're finally awake.</i>

29
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:22,248
<i>Hold on, I'll fix you some breakfast.</i>

30
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:23,458
[Damian] <i>I'm sorry, Dante.</i>

31
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:26,753
<i>Looks like I won't just be</i>
<i>reclaiming Jaguar's identity.</i>

32
00:01:26,836 --> 00:01:30,507
<i>I'll be taking Camia's love</i>
<i>from you, as well.</i>

33
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:32,550
[Loring] <i>Vote at the elections tomorrow.</i>

34
00:01:32,634 --> 00:01:39,808
<i>The voices of the people</i>
<i>of Ardiente need to be heard.</i>

35
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:40,850
[Diego] <i>Get out of here</i>

36
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:43,353
<i>if you don't want to ruin</i>
<i>Julio Ardiente's name.</i>

37
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:52,487
[Diego] Slowly, Uncle.

38
00:01:58,409 --> 00:02:00,203
[Pandoy groaning] Thank you.

39
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:03,498
[exhales]

40
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:10,046
They've gone too far.

41
00:02:11,589 --> 00:02:13,299
They're abusing us.

42
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:16,761
They've gone too far!

43
00:02:18,763 --> 00:02:20,932
I won't… I won't let them
get away with this!

44
00:02:21,015 --> 00:02:22,392
Diego, stop.

45
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:25,895
Don't let everything our supporters
worked hard for go to waste

46
00:02:25,979 --> 00:02:28,148
by going to the Ardientes' place alone.

47
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:30,400
First, it was Aunt Camia.

48
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:32,277
This time, they went after
you and Uncle Pandoy.

49
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,445
Who will they target next? Tell me.

50
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:35,530
Which of us will be next?

51
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:37,824
Diego, the election is in two days.

52
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:40,535
If they won't cheat, I know you'll win.

53
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:42,328
So we need to watch
this election carefully.

54
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:45,999
[Jepoy] She's right, Diego.
We will support you.

55
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:48,501
That's right. This will be over soon.

56
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:53,965
[tense music playing]

57
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:09,564
Thank you, Jaguar, but I need
to go back to the mansion

58
00:03:09,647 --> 00:03:11,858
to find out the truth about my mother.

59
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:31,961
<i>If I give you what you want,</i>
<i>you might decide to stay.</i>

60
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:36,216
<i>But, if I reveal my identity to you…</i>

61
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:47,435
<i>how can I be sure that you won't leave me?</i>

62
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,775
[Ivy] Yes, Congressman?

63
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:57,487
Sit down. Sit down, Ivy.

64
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:03,451
Um…

65
00:04:04,994 --> 00:04:06,913
Sanggano here tells me…

66
00:04:08,539 --> 00:04:14,379
that you didn't help him
in finding the money Diego took.

67
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:18,675
Instead, you just went on your own way.

68
00:04:19,842 --> 00:04:21,010
It makes me wonder…

69
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,472
where did the money go?

70
00:04:24,555 --> 00:04:27,433
[unsettling music playing]

71
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:28,434
Does Diego have it?

72
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:31,938
Or do you?

73
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:34,232
[scoffs]

74
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:41,030
So just because Col. Sanggano said that,

75
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:44,075
you already think I'm going
against you, Congressman?

76
00:04:49,038 --> 00:04:50,623
It's my money, Congressman.

77
00:04:52,041 --> 00:04:54,085
You can have my company
investigated if you want,

78
00:04:54,168 --> 00:04:56,796
but you won't find
the 50 million pesos there.

79
00:04:59,257 --> 00:05:01,467
Just because he failed to catch Diego,

80
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:04,345
Col. Sanggano's already making up stories.

81
00:05:04,429 --> 00:05:06,472
So now, you're suddenly blaming me.

82
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:07,890
Oh. No, no.

83
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:11,644
I'm not blaming you.
I'm not pointing fingers.

84
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:14,772
I just want to make sure

85
00:05:14,856 --> 00:05:18,067
that I still have your loyalty,
Miss Aguas.

86
00:05:20,194 --> 00:05:23,990
You shouldn't question
my loyalty, Congressman.

87
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,284
You have my utmost loyalty.

88
00:05:27,535 --> 00:05:28,703
[inhales deeply]

89
00:05:29,078 --> 00:05:33,374
I'm not like your daughter,
who's ready to betray you.

90
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,460
[laughs]

91
00:05:37,253 --> 00:05:44,010
It takes intelligent people
to mount a plot of revenge.

92
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:46,179
And clearly,

93
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:51,726
Emilia does not have the mettle
for it even if she wanted to.

94
00:05:51,809 --> 00:05:52,894
[chuckles]

95
00:05:54,353 --> 00:05:58,107
Well, Congressman, she surprised me.

96
00:05:58,941 --> 00:06:01,694
I thought Emilia wasn't
an intelligent woman.

97
00:06:02,361 --> 00:06:04,781
But I was wrong.

98
00:06:06,532 --> 00:06:11,704
Do you want me to tell you
who helped her escape?

99
00:06:14,248 --> 00:06:16,751
No need to stand, Congressman.

100
00:06:20,129 --> 00:06:26,969
The one who helped Emilia escape
was no other than…

101
00:06:33,017 --> 00:06:34,060
Jaguar.

102
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:36,562
[tense music intensifies]

103
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:38,022
It's Jaguar.

104
00:06:40,733 --> 00:06:44,445
They've been talking, meeting,

105
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:47,949
and planning to take you down
for a while now.

106
00:06:52,453 --> 00:06:55,248
Well, if you still have doubts…

107
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:01,045
Take a look at this.

108
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:02,755
Proof.

109
00:07:04,423 --> 00:07:06,634
After you look at it, Congressman,

110
00:07:07,552 --> 00:07:11,264
I'll let you decide whether
you'll believe in me

111
00:07:11,347 --> 00:07:13,307
or in Col. Sanggano here.

112
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:23,484
Oh! Happy watching!

113
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:29,866
Colonel, give me that.

114
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:32,660
[suspenseful music playing]

115
00:07:47,925 --> 00:07:49,177
-[man] <i>Boss Jaguar.</i>
-[man 2] <i>Boss.</i>

116
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,261
[Emilia] <i>Jaguar.</i>

117
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,767
[suspenseful music intensifies]

118
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:57,894
[gunshot]

119
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:01,439
Shut that infernal thing down!

120
00:08:03,566 --> 00:08:06,986
Oh! Emilia, Emilia!

121
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:09,113
How could you?!

122
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:11,866
You slimy snake!

123
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:16,370
<i>That Jaguar guy is just</i>
<i>fooling you, Emilia.</i>

124
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:19,874
<i>Papa, that's why I need</i>
<i>to meet up with him,</i>

125
00:08:19,957 --> 00:08:22,543
<i>so I can turn the tables on him.</i>

126
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:24,837
<i>I want you to kill him,</i>

127
00:08:24,921 --> 00:08:26,964
<i>so I won't have any more problems.</i>

128
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:28,591
<i>Okay, Papa.</i>

129
00:08:28,674 --> 00:08:31,177
<i>I'll do exactly what you want me to do.</i>

130
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:33,012
[Julio] <i>I would like you to take care of</i>

131
00:08:33,095 --> 00:08:34,805
<i>one of our enemies.</i>

132
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:36,224
<i>Kill Jaguar.</i>

133
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:39,936
<i>For the sake of our family.</i>

134
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:45,650
[unsettling music playing]

135
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:02,667
Jaguar.

136
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:09,465
Emilia, if really do want
to head back home,

137
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,133
then I won't stop you anymore.

138
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:13,719
But, there's something you should know.

139
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:18,182
[suspenseful music swelling]

140
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:29,235
The Ardientes' men!

141
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:33,864
[gunshots]

142
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:36,867
Get inside!

143
00:09:36,951 --> 00:09:39,161
Tell Boss Jaguar we're
being attacked by the Ardientes!

144
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:43,249
[gunshots]

145
00:09:43,332 --> 00:09:44,458
Boss Jaguar!

146
00:09:44,542 --> 00:09:46,002
-We're being attacked…
-Oh my God!

147
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:47,461
-by Julio's men!
-Huh?!

148
00:09:47,670 --> 00:09:48,754
[gunshots]

149
00:09:49,964 --> 00:09:51,716
[gunshots]

150
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:01,058
Emilia, you have to get
out of here! Leave this to us.

151
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:04,353
-I can't just leave you here!
-There's no time! Just go!

152
00:10:04,437 --> 00:10:06,147
-Jaguar, no!
-Give me the gun!

153
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:08,524
No, Jaguar! Jaguar!

154
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:12,194
-Come with us, Emilia Torillo!
-[exclaims] Let go of me!

155
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:14,280
[grunts] I said, let go!

156
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:17,450
-[Emilia] Papa? Papa!
-[Julio] Hmm?

157
00:10:17,533 --> 00:10:19,285
[Julio] That's close enough.

158
00:10:20,911 --> 00:10:21,912
[Julio scoffs]

159
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:28,252
Fancy seeing you here, Emilia.

160
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:30,671
You know what?

161
00:10:31,672 --> 00:10:33,966
I've been waiting for you
since the other day

162
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:36,385
you promised to come over.

163
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:39,680
But, for some reason, you never showed up.

164
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:43,142
But then, I realized…

165
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:48,022
My daughter must be enjoying
herself at her new house.

166
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:54,320
Spending time with her new
live-in partner,

167
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:55,655
also known as…

168
00:10:59,116 --> 00:11:00,117
Jaguar?

169
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:07,458
[stutters] Papa, let me explain.

170
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:09,251
[Julio shouts] There's nothing to discuss!

171
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:18,594
Jaguar was the one who helped you escape.

172
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:23,099
You have been working with him all along!

173
00:11:23,849 --> 00:11:25,393
I remembered! I remembered!

174
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:28,854
I asked you countless times for his head!

175
00:11:28,938 --> 00:11:30,314
Countless times!

176
00:11:30,398 --> 00:11:32,108
But you never delivered.

177
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:34,443
And now, I know why.

178
00:11:34,527 --> 00:11:36,445
Because you're nothing but a slut

179
00:11:36,529 --> 00:11:39,281
who's been fooling
around with that bastard!

180
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:43,994
You're worse than a dog in heat!

181
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:46,872
I'm sorry, Papa.

182
00:11:47,415 --> 00:11:50,376
I'm sorry, please forgive me.

183
00:11:50,459 --> 00:11:52,169
I'm sorry.

184
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:53,504
Get out!

185
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:58,175
Sorry! Sorry! I'm sorry, Papa!

186
00:11:58,259 --> 00:11:59,718
Get yourself out of here
before I kill you!

187
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,053
No! No, Papa!

188
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:03,347
-Get out of my house!
-[Emilia] No…

189
00:12:03,431 --> 00:12:06,767
And never set foot in this house again!

190
00:12:06,851 --> 00:12:10,563
I forbid you!
Don't set foot in this house!

191
00:12:11,439 --> 00:12:13,357
Please, Papa! Forgive me!

192
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,651
And now, you wonder, you seriously wonder,

193
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:17,695
why I never loved you?

194
00:12:18,946 --> 00:12:20,865
Take a good look at yourself!

195
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:26,245
This is precisely why
I could not love you!

196
00:12:27,121 --> 00:12:29,498
Because you're no different…

197
00:12:30,749 --> 00:12:32,376
from your treacherous mother!

198
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:34,336
You're just like her!

199
00:12:35,754 --> 00:12:37,798
Get out of my house!

200
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:39,258
-Get out!
-[gunshot]

201
00:12:39,341 --> 00:12:41,260
-Papa!
-Get out of the house!

202
00:12:41,343 --> 00:12:43,512
[wailing] Papa!

203
00:12:44,346 --> 00:12:47,016
-Get out!
-Papa!

204
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:52,021
-[Julio sobs]
-[tense music intensifies]

205
00:12:56,484 --> 00:13:01,155
<i>Emilia Ardiente-Torillo,</i>
<i>the second person on my list.</i>

206
00:13:01,822 --> 00:13:05,159
<i>I swore to myself</i>
<i>I'd make your father disown you.</i>

207
00:13:05,242 --> 00:13:09,038
<i>That you'd be stripped</i>
<i>of both your title and your dignity.</i>

208
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:11,332
<i>Mission accomplished.</i>

209
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:17,213
<i>As they say, the most dangerous foe</i>

210
00:13:17,838 --> 00:13:19,924
<i>is the one who pretends to be a friend.</i>

211
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:23,093
<i>That's the lesson</i>
<i>you'll be learning in the end,</i>

212
00:13:23,177 --> 00:13:27,223
<i>because you're next on my list,</i>
<i>Julio Ardiente.</i>

213
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:30,976
I'm here for you, Congressman.

214
00:13:36,857 --> 00:13:38,317
Papa!

215
00:13:40,361 --> 00:13:41,362
[sobs]

216
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:42,821
Papa!

217
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:52,373
[Julio] <i>Take a good look at yourself!</i>

218
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:56,752
<i>This is precisely why</i>
<i>I could not love you!</i>

219
00:13:56,835 --> 00:13:59,463
<i>Because you're no different…</i>

220
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:01,549
<i>from your treacherous mother!</i>

221
00:14:07,054 --> 00:14:10,391
[monitor beeping rhythmically]

222
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,561
[Julio exhales]

223
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:32,037
So, Congressman…

224
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:36,125
looks like I've proven
my loyalty to you once again.

225
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:39,962
I apologize for doubting you.

226
00:14:42,339 --> 00:14:46,552
I should've known not to expect
anything else from Emilia

227
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:49,221
other than failure and betrayal.

228
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:55,769
Miss Ivy Aguas…

229
00:14:58,188 --> 00:15:01,650
From this day forward, we only
have each other to rely on.

230
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:04,945
So, let's not screw it up.

231
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:11,160
Do you really have to keep reminding me

232
00:15:11,243 --> 00:15:14,371
not to break your trust?

233
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:20,377
Congressman Julio,
you should know by now that

234
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:23,547
I'm the strongest ally you have left.

235
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:27,676
Now, it's my turn to remind you, Julio.

236
00:15:28,677 --> 00:15:30,679
Don't try me, Congressman.

237
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:34,725
[tense music swelling]

238
00:15:52,242 --> 00:15:53,243
Jaguar!

239
00:15:54,536 --> 00:15:56,288
Those are Papa's men.

240
00:15:57,122 --> 00:15:58,791
Where are you, Jaguar?

241
00:15:58,874 --> 00:16:00,668
[man laughs]

242
00:16:01,543 --> 00:16:04,046
[suspenseful music playing]

243
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:05,422
Jaguar.

244
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:07,549
Boss Jaguar,

245
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:09,969
Julio's men are still at our headquarters.

246
00:16:12,012 --> 00:16:13,597
-[thumps]
-[exhales]

247
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:18,727
Looks like those pests
don't plan to leave.

248
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:23,941
I think it's time
to look for a new hideout.

249
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:42,876
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

250
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,628
<i>Please try again later.</i>

251
00:16:44,962 --> 00:16:45,963
[sets phone down]

252
00:16:46,046 --> 00:16:47,965
[tense music playing]

253
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:52,553
[upbeat drums music playing]

254
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:08,110
[music continues]

255
00:17:10,362 --> 00:17:12,406
[camera shutters click]

256
00:17:19,163 --> 00:17:20,330
[Loring] Just a few more hours.

257
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:24,168
Diego, this is the day
we've been waiting for.

258
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:28,380
Though I can't say I'm fine
with accepting defeat.

259
00:17:28,464 --> 00:17:30,883
Because I believe
you're going to be the winner.

260
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:33,135
I know you're meant to be the governor.

261
00:17:33,218 --> 00:17:34,303
That's right!

262
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:41,685
That's right… I will be
the governor of this town.

263
00:17:42,936 --> 00:17:44,813
For a new Ardiente!

264
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:47,066
[all] To the new Ardiente!

265
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:51,862
-[cheers and applause]
-Diego!

266
00:17:51,945 --> 00:17:57,159
[all] Go Diego! Go Diego! Go Diego!

267
00:17:57,242 --> 00:18:02,081
Go Diego! Go Diego! Go Diego!

268
00:18:02,164 --> 00:18:07,544
Go Diego! Go Diego! Go Diego!

269
00:18:08,837 --> 00:18:10,339
Is that your

270
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:11,757
<i>final price?</i>

271
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:16,345
I think you're putting too
much value on your position

272
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:19,515
as Election Commissioner Secretary.

273
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:22,267
<i>Leandro Marquez.</i>

274
00:18:22,351 --> 00:18:23,977
Congressman, if you really
want to win, then,

275
00:18:24,061 --> 00:18:25,354
you have to make the investment.

276
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:27,564
<i>Besides, I'm sure you'll earn back</i>

277
00:18:27,648 --> 00:18:30,901
whatever you invested once
you're governor, correct?

278
00:18:31,568 --> 00:18:32,861
I'll think about it.

279
00:18:33,821 --> 00:18:34,947
I'll call you back.

280
00:18:35,489 --> 00:18:37,032
Sure. I'm only one call

281
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:38,158
<i>away, Congressman.</i>

282
00:18:38,742 --> 00:18:40,869
One call away from your victory.

283
00:18:44,498 --> 00:18:46,625
You bloodsucking leech!

284
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:52,548
Colonel, I have a plan.

285
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:56,677
And in this plan,
my victory will be certain.

286
00:18:57,427 --> 00:19:02,141
We won't have to bribe anyone
or negotiate with anybody.

287
00:19:03,642 --> 00:19:05,352
We'll just have to blow things up.

288
00:19:06,645 --> 00:19:09,982
So that people against me can't vote.

289
00:19:10,065 --> 00:19:11,441
[suspenseful music]

290
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:12,526
[scoffs]

291
00:19:24,746 --> 00:19:26,123
Excuse me. Can I use your phone?

292
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:27,457
I need to use your phone.

293
00:19:27,916 --> 00:19:29,293
Ten pesos for a call.

294
00:19:34,756 --> 00:19:37,259
Don't demand something
if you can't pay for it.

295
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:38,760
How dare you!

296
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:40,596
Don't you know that I can buy your store?

297
00:19:40,679 --> 00:19:42,389
I can even buy you.

298
00:19:42,472 --> 00:19:45,475
So-- Ew, don't touch me! Gross.

299
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:47,644
Who do you think you are?

300
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:52,858
Wait, aren't you the former governor?

301
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:56,653
Yes. I am Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.

302
00:19:56,737 --> 00:20:00,032
Now, maybe you can let me use your phone?

303
00:20:00,115 --> 00:20:01,867
Aren't you supposed to be in jail?

304
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:02,951
Wait.

305
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:06,705
Hey! Hey, get back here!

306
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:27,351
-Welcome.
-Thank you.

307
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:41,615
Ma'am, here's your bill.

308
00:20:54,836 --> 00:20:56,463
Where's your restroom?

309
00:20:56,546 --> 00:20:58,173
-Over there.
-There?

310
00:20:58,257 --> 00:20:59,383
-Yes.
-Okay. Thank you.

311
00:20:59,466 --> 00:21:00,759
-Sure.
-Thank you very much.

312
00:21:07,432 --> 00:21:10,310
-[Emilia exclaims]
-Ma'am! Ma'am! Ma'am!

313
00:21:10,394 --> 00:21:14,273
[suspenseful music playing]

314
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:42,009
[suspenseful music continues]

315
00:21:55,605 --> 00:21:57,274
[truck engine starts]

316
00:21:57,733 --> 00:22:03,071
[suspenseful music continues]

317
00:22:15,459 --> 00:22:17,961
[news anchor] <i>And in</i>
<i>Poblacion Ardiente news,</i>

318
00:22:18,462 --> 00:22:20,172
<i>the first batch of voting machines</i>

319
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:21,840
<i>just arrived last night.</i>

320
00:22:21,923 --> 00:22:25,635
<i>They will be used by 10</i>
<i>of the province's towns.</i>

321
00:22:28,388 --> 00:22:30,891
<i>And this morning, the remaining towns</i>

322
00:22:30,974 --> 00:22:33,810
<i>will be receiving their voting machines.</i>

323
00:22:36,438 --> 00:22:38,440
[Julio] <i>My victory will be certain.</i>

324
00:22:38,523 --> 00:22:43,361
<i>We won't have to bribe anyone</i>
<i>or negotiate with anybody.</i>

325
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:45,155
<i>We'll just have to blow things up.</i>

326
00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:53,580
-What's happening?
-I've been here for hours.

327
00:22:53,663 --> 00:22:56,666
-It's been delayed for so long.
-[voters clamoring]

328
00:22:56,750 --> 00:22:58,752
[election officer 1] I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

329
00:22:58,835 --> 00:23:00,670
We're having some technical problems!

330
00:23:00,754 --> 00:23:03,590
-Don't tell me it's what I think it is.
-Wait. You can't vote yet.

331
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:06,468
The voting machines
from Manila got delayed.

332
00:23:06,551 --> 00:23:08,887
-Really?
-When are they arriving?

333
00:23:08,970 --> 00:23:10,180
-Let's just be patient.
-Miss…

334
00:23:10,263 --> 00:23:12,724
the other towns have already voted.

335
00:23:12,808 --> 00:23:14,351
-Meanwhile, we've been here for hours.
-Yeah.

336
00:23:14,434 --> 00:23:16,019
-Please don't worry.
-And we still haven't voted yet.

337
00:23:16,103 --> 00:23:18,855
The voting machines are
arriving, they're on their way.

338
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:20,565
-But when?
-They're coming from Manila?!

339
00:23:20,649 --> 00:23:22,442
-Yes, on its way.
-We have somewhere else to be.

340
00:23:22,526 --> 00:23:24,402
-You'll be able to vote.
-We never know what's happening.

341
00:23:24,486 --> 00:23:25,445
[woman] Geez!

342
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:27,531
They might blow up the truck.

343
00:23:27,614 --> 00:23:29,157
The same one carrying voting machines

344
00:23:29,241 --> 00:23:30,367
that are coming in from Manila.

345
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:32,369
-What?
-Diego, a lot of voters

346
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:35,580
won't be able to vote
if they blow up the machines.

347
00:23:39,584 --> 00:23:40,877
I've got an idea. Come with me.

348
00:23:53,807 --> 00:23:56,893
I bet the truck from Manila
definitely has a bomb.

349
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:59,563
One that can be detonated
with a cell phone.

350
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:02,149
If it's really from Manila,

351
00:24:02,232 --> 00:24:04,442
a checkpoint would have spotted the bomb.

352
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:08,572
My guess is they'll plant
the bomb here in Ardiente.

353
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:12,409
Let's just follow them.

354
00:24:14,077 --> 00:24:16,788
[suspenseful music playing]

355
00:24:50,822 --> 00:24:54,159
[suspenseful music continues]

356
00:24:54,993 --> 00:24:56,661
Let's go! Hurry!

357
00:25:12,052 --> 00:25:14,054
[explosion]

358
00:25:23,104 --> 00:25:24,105
[Diego] Are you okay?

359
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:35,033
-Are you all right?
-I'm fine.

360
00:25:40,288 --> 00:25:42,290
[reporter 1] <i>It was revealed</i>
<i>that the voting machines</i>

361
00:25:42,374 --> 00:25:44,209
<i>which exploded were</i>
<i>supposed to be delivered</i>

362
00:25:44,292 --> 00:25:46,127
<i>to the neighborhood where a majority</i>

363
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:48,964
<i>of Diego Torillo's supporters reside.</i>

364
00:25:49,756 --> 00:25:52,467
<i>And now, we're here</i>
<i>with Mr. Diego Torillo.</i>

365
00:25:52,550 --> 00:25:55,053
<i>Mr. Diego Torillo, what can</i>
<i>you say about what happened?</i>

366
00:25:55,136 --> 00:25:59,057
<i>I'm sure that the Ardientes</i>
<i>are responsible for this.</i>

367
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:00,392
[Diego] <i>They bombed the truck</i>

368
00:26:00,475 --> 00:26:01,977
<i>that was supposed</i>
<i>to deliver voting machines</i>

369
00:26:02,060 --> 00:26:04,187
<i>to the neighborhood where</i>
<i>most of my supporters reside.</i>

370
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:08,149
<i>It's so obvious that they are</i>
<i>trying to sabotage my votes.</i>

371
00:26:09,526 --> 00:26:11,403
[Charlie] <i>Thank you, Mr. Diego Torillo.</i>

372
00:26:11,987 --> 00:26:14,281
<i>With the explosion of the said</i>
<i>voting machines,</i>

373
00:26:14,364 --> 00:26:18,410
<i>will it be a victory for Julio Ardiente?</i>

374
00:26:18,493 --> 00:26:20,578
<i>And is it true that</i>
<i>the Ardientes are responsible</i>

375
00:26:20,662 --> 00:26:22,080
<i>for the explosion?</i>

376
00:26:22,163 --> 00:26:23,331
<i>Stay tuned for updates.</i>

377
00:26:23,415 --> 00:26:25,875
<i>This is Charlie Costanilla, reporting.</i>

378
00:26:25,959 --> 00:26:29,754
What a brilliant plan!

379
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:32,966
Son of a gun, Julio!

380
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:34,884
You're the bomb.

381
00:26:34,968 --> 00:26:38,221
Ivy, does this mean
the election will be postponed?

382
00:26:38,930 --> 00:26:40,932
If so, that old man will definitely win!

383
00:26:41,266 --> 00:26:43,351
Mom, they can't postpone the election.

384
00:26:44,477 --> 00:26:48,064
Don't worry. Diego is already
doing everything he can.

385
00:26:48,648 --> 00:26:52,027
Julio can't sabotage our votes.

386
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:55,030
Diego is making sure that won't happen.

387
00:26:55,113 --> 00:26:56,114
[door opens]

388
00:26:58,325 --> 00:26:59,451
[door closes]

389
00:26:59,534 --> 00:27:02,329
Lily. Been there long?

390
00:27:03,872 --> 00:27:06,166
Uh. Uncle, I just arrived.

391
00:27:06,249 --> 00:27:07,250
Have you eaten?

392
00:27:15,258 --> 00:27:18,470
Mom, can we talk in private?

393
00:27:28,855 --> 00:27:29,856
Lily.

394
00:27:31,649 --> 00:27:33,109
What did you want to talk about?

395
00:27:34,944 --> 00:27:36,488
Mom, it's Uncle Damian.

396
00:27:37,489 --> 00:27:38,531
He escaped.

397
00:27:39,657 --> 00:27:41,368
He was never released from jail.

398
00:27:42,952 --> 00:27:44,371
Mom, you need to be careful.

399
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:46,164
I think it was a bad idea to take him in

400
00:27:46,247 --> 00:27:48,041
and take care of him.

401
00:27:48,124 --> 00:27:49,959
It's dangerous for you.

402
00:27:50,043 --> 00:27:53,254
Your uncle said that he's a changed man

403
00:27:53,338 --> 00:27:55,090
and that he runs a business in Manila.

404
00:27:55,173 --> 00:27:59,052
Mom, if he lied about his escape,

405
00:27:59,135 --> 00:28:01,513
maybe we shouldn't trust him so much.

406
00:28:04,349 --> 00:28:05,433
You're right, Lily.

407
00:28:06,768 --> 00:28:09,104
But we can't just ask him to leave

408
00:28:09,187 --> 00:28:11,189
when his injuries haven't healed.

409
00:28:11,731 --> 00:28:13,066
He needs us.

410
00:28:14,317 --> 00:28:16,486
Mom, I'm just worried about you.

411
00:28:17,821 --> 00:28:18,947
You need to be careful.

412
00:28:20,657 --> 00:28:21,658
[phone dings]

413
00:28:26,830 --> 00:28:29,124
Julio just texted. I need to go.

414
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:31,793
Thank you, dear.

415
00:28:31,876 --> 00:28:33,586
And don't worry. I'll be careful.

416
00:28:41,803 --> 00:28:42,804
See you soon.

417
00:28:46,474 --> 00:28:47,475
[exhales]

418
00:29:00,530 --> 00:29:02,532
[tense music playing]

419
00:29:28,933 --> 00:29:29,684
[mouths] Thank you.

420
00:29:29,768 --> 00:29:33,855
[tense music continues playing]

421
00:29:46,242 --> 00:29:49,954
[supporters] Ardiente! Ardiente!
Ardiente! Ardiente!

422
00:29:50,038 --> 00:29:53,458
Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

423
00:29:53,541 --> 00:29:57,545
Ardiente! Ardiente!
Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

424
00:29:57,629 --> 00:29:59,798
[election officer 2] Silence, please!

425
00:29:59,881 --> 00:30:03,301
Be considerate of other voters!

426
00:30:03,384 --> 00:30:06,596
Voters, please fall in line properly!

427
00:30:06,679 --> 00:30:08,890
[election officer 1] I'm sorry.
Please wait outside.

428
00:30:08,973 --> 00:30:10,391
We haven't set up.

429
00:30:10,475 --> 00:30:12,769
-Come on. Hurry.
-When will the machines arrive?

430
00:30:12,852 --> 00:30:14,020
[election officer 1] Please wait for them.

431
00:30:14,103 --> 00:30:15,480
The other neighborhood has
already cast its votes.

432
00:30:15,563 --> 00:30:16,439
[woman 1] Yeah.

433
00:30:16,523 --> 00:30:18,191
Meanwhile, we've been here for hours,

434
00:30:18,274 --> 00:30:20,109
but voting still hasn't started!

435
00:30:21,945 --> 00:30:22,779
What's wrong?

436
00:30:22,862 --> 00:30:23,947
-Isn't it?
-[woman 1] That's true.

437
00:30:24,030 --> 00:30:24,781
Wait. Wait.

438
00:30:24,864 --> 00:30:25,990
[Loring] How come they're already set up?

439
00:30:26,074 --> 00:30:27,867
What's going on? What's happening?

440
00:30:27,951 --> 00:30:29,369
-We apologize.
-What time is it?

441
00:30:29,452 --> 00:30:30,870
What's going on here?

442
00:30:30,954 --> 00:30:32,956
The voting machines for our
neighborhood haven't arrived.

443
00:30:33,039 --> 00:30:33,873
Please be patient.

444
00:30:33,957 --> 00:30:34,874
-We're wasting time!
-Oh, good grief.

445
00:30:34,958 --> 00:30:36,167
[man] What is that?

446
00:30:36,251 --> 00:30:38,461
-What… what is that?
-[man] What's happening now?

447
00:30:38,545 --> 00:30:41,673
Look! They've already set up.

448
00:30:41,756 --> 00:30:42,966
What happened to our voting machines?

449
00:30:43,049 --> 00:30:46,094
I have a bad feeling about this!

450
00:30:46,177 --> 00:30:47,720
Look! They're almost done!

451
00:30:47,804 --> 00:30:48,721
I know, Auntie.

452
00:30:48,805 --> 00:30:50,223
[man] I know this is on purpose…

453
00:30:50,306 --> 00:30:53,977
No one else is capable of doing
this other than Julio Ardiente.

454
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:55,520
This can't be!

455
00:30:56,688 --> 00:30:58,147
We can't just keep waiting here.

456
00:30:58,231 --> 00:31:00,775
We can't just stand here and do nothing.

457
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:03,611
Look! We all came here to vote!

458
00:31:03,695 --> 00:31:05,989
We should demand our rights
and ask the government

459
00:31:06,072 --> 00:31:08,908
to give us a chance to vote…

460
00:31:08,992 --> 00:31:09,909
That's right! Yeah!

461
00:31:09,993 --> 00:31:12,120
…with or without the machines!

462
00:31:12,203 --> 00:31:12,996
Yeah!

463
00:31:13,079 --> 00:31:16,165
Right! We need to cast our votes in

464
00:31:16,249 --> 00:31:19,752
for the one who deserves to win,

465
00:31:19,836 --> 00:31:20,879
and that's Diego!

466
00:31:20,962 --> 00:31:22,922
-Diego!
-[applause]

467
00:31:23,006 --> 00:31:24,465
-[man] Diego!
-[applause]

468
00:31:26,342 --> 00:31:30,179
I don't think the congressman
is responsible

469
00:31:30,263 --> 00:31:33,892
for the bombing of the truck
carrying their voting machines.

470
00:31:33,975 --> 00:31:36,060
[woman] I'm sure Diego's
supporters just made that up

471
00:31:36,144 --> 00:31:37,729
because they know that he'll lose.

472
00:31:37,812 --> 00:31:39,272
[scoffs] You're right.

473
00:31:39,355 --> 00:31:41,316
[tense music continues playing]

474
00:31:41,399 --> 00:31:47,030
You know, violence isn't
the key to winning an election.

475
00:31:47,113 --> 00:31:49,240
I'm sure Diego's camp wouldn't do that.

476
00:31:49,949 --> 00:31:51,451
Do you hear what you're saying?

477
00:31:51,534 --> 00:31:53,453
Are you really a supporter
of the Ardientes?

478
00:31:53,536 --> 00:31:56,456
Or is Diego Torillo your bet
for the position of governor?

479
00:31:58,458 --> 00:32:02,545
Young boy, please
don't be rude to Miss Aguas.

480
00:32:04,339 --> 00:32:05,381
Sorry, Congressman.

481
00:32:11,846 --> 00:32:14,557
Mister, I am Ivy Aguas.

482
00:32:14,641 --> 00:32:16,601
I'm one with the Ardientes.

483
00:32:16,684 --> 00:32:19,312
That's why I'm on
the same line as you are.

484
00:32:20,855 --> 00:32:21,856
Sorry, ma'am.

485
00:32:26,027 --> 00:32:29,155
[man] Did you see that?
Wow. Let's just cast our votes.

486
00:32:29,238 --> 00:32:30,949
-Let's just vote.
-Yeah.

487
00:32:49,092 --> 00:32:50,301
[indistinct chatter]

488
00:32:57,976 --> 00:32:59,435
[tense music continues playing]

489
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:01,270
[election officer]
Here's the voting machine.

490
00:33:04,649 --> 00:33:05,775
[indistinct chatter]

491
00:33:07,568 --> 00:33:10,905
[tense music continues playing]

492
00:33:16,285 --> 00:33:22,375
[supporters] Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

493
00:33:22,458 --> 00:33:24,168
[man] Long live the Ardientes!

494
00:33:24,836 --> 00:33:30,633
[overlapping chants]

495
00:33:30,717 --> 00:33:35,722
[supporters] Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

496
00:33:35,805 --> 00:33:39,350
Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

497
00:33:39,434 --> 00:33:43,021
Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

498
00:33:43,104 --> 00:33:46,649
Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

499
00:33:46,733 --> 00:33:50,570
Ardiente! Ardiente! Ardiente!

500
00:33:50,653 --> 00:33:55,658
-Long live the Congressman!
-Long live!

501
00:33:55,742 --> 00:33:59,287
-Long live!
-Long live the Ardientes!

502
00:33:59,370 --> 00:34:00,788
[man] Long live Ardiente!

503
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:03,291
[music fading]

504
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:07,503
[tense music playing]

505
00:34:09,964 --> 00:34:11,174
[Julio clears throat]

506
00:34:11,257 --> 00:34:12,133
Diego Torillo.

507
00:34:15,553 --> 00:34:16,846
Where is your…

508
00:34:18,765 --> 00:34:20,099
white flag?

509
00:34:20,975 --> 00:34:23,936
Didn't you come here to surrender?

510
00:34:24,812 --> 00:34:26,522
I know you were behind the explosion.

511
00:34:27,732 --> 00:34:30,777
But no matter what you do,
you will never succeed.

512
00:34:34,322 --> 00:34:37,784
Julio, if you win,
our people will be lucky

513
00:34:37,867 --> 00:34:40,995
if you decide to share the money
your family plundered.

514
00:34:41,329 --> 00:34:43,748
But we all know you would never do that.

515
00:34:44,707 --> 00:34:47,460
Because for you,
there are only two solutions.

516
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:50,004
Violence and murder.

517
00:34:51,547 --> 00:34:53,049
[Diego] That is why…

518
00:34:53,132 --> 00:34:56,928
we will never allow someone
like you to lead this province.

519
00:34:57,762 --> 00:34:58,846
[chuckles]

520
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:02,058
The two of you are so self-righteous.

521
00:35:02,141 --> 00:35:07,021
How can you be sure
I was behind the explosion?

522
00:35:07,855 --> 00:35:12,235
What do I care if someone
blew up the voting machines?

523
00:35:12,318 --> 00:35:15,029
It'll barely have an effect
on the results.

524
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:17,156
Besides, those votes weren't all for you.

525
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:18,741
You two are a little too self-assured.

526
00:35:18,825 --> 00:35:20,159
Julio!

527
00:35:20,243 --> 00:35:21,786
Forty percent of voters

528
00:35:21,869 --> 00:35:24,372
won't be able to vote
because of the explosion.

529
00:35:24,997 --> 00:35:26,290
But don't worry.

530
00:35:27,083 --> 00:35:30,336
We're doing everything we can
to get new voting machines,

531
00:35:30,419 --> 00:35:31,629
so we can vote.

532
00:35:33,005 --> 00:35:34,298
[Diego] We would rather die…

533
00:35:35,049 --> 00:35:38,052
than leave Poblacion Ardiente
in your hands.

534
00:35:39,345 --> 00:35:41,472
And before I die,

535
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:46,477
I'll make sure that
this town will not fall

536
00:35:46,561 --> 00:35:48,563
into the hands of someone like you.

537
00:35:48,646 --> 00:35:50,523
Julio, your time is up.

538
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:53,359
Because I'll make sure that
from this day on,

539
00:35:53,442 --> 00:35:56,612
evil will no longer reign in Ardiente.

540
00:35:58,823 --> 00:35:59,991
[Diego] Excuse me.

541
00:36:00,074 --> 00:36:03,494
[tense music playing]

542
00:36:14,255 --> 00:36:15,214
Auntie…

543
00:36:16,716 --> 00:36:17,842
I'll just go over there.

544
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:21,596
[indistinct chatter]

545
00:36:21,679 --> 00:36:22,680
[Anna] Diego.

546
00:36:23,222 --> 00:36:24,599
[Loring] Diego.

547
00:36:24,682 --> 00:36:29,061
The sun's about to set,
and we still haven't voted!

548
00:36:29,145 --> 00:36:31,022
The machines aren't even here yet.

549
00:36:31,105 --> 00:36:32,398
What are we going to do?

550
00:36:32,940 --> 00:36:35,109
Miss Camia, the voting machines are here.

551
00:36:35,193 --> 00:36:36,152
We can set them up now.

552
00:36:36,235 --> 00:36:37,361
-They are?
-Yes.

553
00:36:37,445 --> 00:36:38,654
That's good to hear.

554
00:36:38,738 --> 00:36:40,031
Don't worry, Nanny.

555
00:36:40,114 --> 00:36:43,284
Everyone, if the voting machines
don't arrive today,

556
00:36:43,367 --> 00:36:45,745
I'll make sure you all get to vote

557
00:36:45,828 --> 00:36:47,079
first thing tomorrow morning.

558
00:36:47,163 --> 00:36:50,416
-Thank you!
-Just don't lose hope!

559
00:36:52,627 --> 00:36:56,047
Miss Loring! Everyone.
I have some good news!

560
00:37:09,602 --> 00:37:10,770
[line rings]

561
00:37:11,270 --> 00:37:14,982
Martel! What is this?

562
00:37:15,066 --> 00:37:18,861
Well?! What are these new
voting machines I'm seeing?

563
00:37:18,945 --> 00:37:20,655
<i>Didn't we talk about this?</i>

564
00:37:20,738 --> 00:37:22,865
And now, I see two of them

565
00:37:22,949 --> 00:37:25,409
being set up directly
in my rival's polling place?!

566
00:37:25,493 --> 00:37:27,370
Oh. Here come the voting machines!

567
00:37:27,453 --> 00:37:28,829
-Hooray!
-Now, we can vote!

568
00:37:28,913 --> 00:37:30,873
[crowd cheering, whooping]

569
00:37:30,957 --> 00:37:33,793
-Come one, let's line up!
-We can now vote!

570
00:37:33,876 --> 00:37:36,087
The public is keeping a close eye on us.

571
00:37:36,754 --> 00:37:39,423
They think the Ardientes
are very corrupt and violent.

572
00:37:40,258 --> 00:37:41,259
Corrupt?

573
00:37:42,551 --> 00:37:43,594
Violent?

574
00:37:44,136 --> 00:37:46,013
Are you out of your mind?!

575
00:37:46,847 --> 00:37:48,766
Haven't you seen the statistics?

576
00:37:49,350 --> 00:37:53,854
Poblacion Ardiente has a zero crime rate!

577
00:37:53,938 --> 00:37:57,108
Nobody believes that blatant
lie anymore, Julio.

578
00:37:57,692 --> 00:37:59,151
<i>You should know better.</i>

579
00:37:59,235 --> 00:38:00,278
<i>But that being said,</i>

580
00:38:00,361 --> 00:38:03,698
the whole country is focused
on the result of that election.

581
00:38:03,781 --> 00:38:07,910
<i>If I don't give in to the public's demand</i>
<i>for new voting machines,</i>

582
00:38:07,994 --> 00:38:11,414
it'll be another point against you.

583
00:38:13,249 --> 00:38:14,875
Son of a gun!

584
00:38:22,675 --> 00:38:24,635
[applause]

585
00:38:24,719 --> 00:38:26,887
[cheering and whooping]

586
00:38:26,971 --> 00:38:28,222
[Diego] Let's go, everyone!

587
00:38:28,306 --> 00:38:30,808
-[cheering and whooping]
-[Pandoy] It's here!

588
00:38:30,891 --> 00:38:32,601
[election officer 1]
Let's line up everyone.

589
00:38:32,685 --> 00:38:36,689
-[applause]
-[overlapping chatter]

590
00:38:36,772 --> 00:38:38,899
You're going to be the governor for sure!

591
00:38:38,983 --> 00:38:42,320
[cheering and whooping]

592
00:38:45,531 --> 00:38:47,325
Everybody! Let's line up!

593
00:38:47,408 --> 00:38:48,993
[Loring] Let's go! Come on!

594
00:38:49,744 --> 00:38:51,412
[cheers and laughter]

595
00:38:51,829 --> 00:38:55,333
[cheering and chattering continue]

596
00:38:55,416 --> 00:38:59,045
[soft music playing]

597
00:38:59,128 --> 00:38:59,962
[Anna] Congrats!

598
00:39:00,046 --> 00:39:02,673
[Diego] Let's line up!
Let's line up! Okay! Auntie.

599
00:39:02,757 --> 00:39:03,758
Diego!

600
00:39:07,053 --> 00:39:08,804
Auntie, thank goodness
we can finally vote.

601
00:39:08,888 --> 00:39:10,848
That's because you never give up.

602
00:39:12,350 --> 00:39:13,976
It's because we never give up.

603
00:39:14,685 --> 00:39:15,686
[giggles]

604
00:39:17,104 --> 00:39:18,439
-Let's go, Auntie.
-Let's start.

605
00:39:18,814 --> 00:39:20,232
[Camia giggles]

606
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:24,987
[ominous music]

607
00:39:25,071 --> 00:39:28,074
[upbeat drums music playing]

608
00:39:58,938 --> 00:40:01,816
[music continues]

609
00:40:43,732 --> 00:40:44,775
[music stops]

610
00:40:51,323 --> 00:40:53,033
[reporter] <i>After a long period of waiting,</i>

611
00:40:53,117 --> 00:40:56,495
<i>the citizens of Sto. Niño</i>
<i>were finally able to vote</i>

612
00:40:56,579 --> 00:40:58,622
<i>with the eventual arrival</i>
<i>of new voting machines.</i>

613
00:40:58,706 --> 00:41:00,541
<i>This includes gubernatorial candidate</i>

614
00:41:00,624 --> 00:41:02,126
<i>Diego Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

615
00:41:02,209 --> 00:41:05,045
[tense music playing]

616
00:41:14,555 --> 00:41:18,767
[tense music intensifies]

617
00:41:40,456 --> 00:41:43,792
[Camia] <i>Dante was killed</i>
<i>by the most powerful family</i>

618
00:41:43,876 --> 00:41:47,713
<i>in Poblacion Ardiente years ago.</i>

619
00:41:48,214 --> 00:41:49,715
<i>Emilia Ardiente was the one behind it.</i>

620
00:41:58,849 --> 00:42:02,102
I really shouldn't care whether
or not they killed you.

621
00:42:02,603 --> 00:42:04,063
Now is my chance to have Camia.

622
00:42:06,899 --> 00:42:08,901
[sighs] But, no.

623
00:42:10,986 --> 00:42:13,364
The Ardientes killed my brother.

624
00:42:15,491 --> 00:42:18,994
They killed Dante without mercy!

625
00:42:19,954 --> 00:42:24,250
<i>I want you, Jaguar.</i>
<i>I want to marry you. Please!</i>

626
00:42:26,460 --> 00:42:32,466
<i>If only I'd known how that woman, Emilia,</i>

627
00:42:32,550 --> 00:42:36,053
<i>was the one who had my brother killed,</i>

628
00:42:37,054 --> 00:42:43,227
<i>I wouldn't have let her get out alive</i>
<i>the first time we met.</i>

629
00:42:45,145 --> 00:42:47,856
You, Emilia, are the one responsible

630
00:42:47,940 --> 00:42:50,651
for my brother's death.

631
00:42:52,987 --> 00:42:56,782
I'll make sure you pay for what you did.

632
00:43:04,832 --> 00:43:05,833
[Emilia groaning]

633
00:43:11,338 --> 00:43:12,798
Where is this place?

634
00:43:12,881 --> 00:43:14,800
Can you help me, please, mister?

635
00:43:17,261 --> 00:43:19,054
[groans] My gosh!

636
00:43:20,764 --> 00:43:21,849
Where am I?

637
00:43:25,436 --> 00:43:26,228
Oh.

638
00:43:26,312 --> 00:43:29,857
I want to apologize for riding
in the back of your truck.

639
00:43:29,940 --> 00:43:31,775
It was never my intention.

640
00:43:32,401 --> 00:43:34,862
And, I'm really sorry for that.

641
00:43:34,945 --> 00:43:35,904
[no audible dialogue]

642
00:43:35,988 --> 00:43:37,865
So, if you'll excuse me, please.

643
00:43:42,119 --> 00:43:43,746
Thanks for these too.

644
00:43:53,213 --> 00:43:55,758
[whooping] I'm in Manila!

645
00:43:56,800 --> 00:43:59,678
[laughs] And I still haven't
gotten caught!

646
00:44:00,262 --> 00:44:01,889
Isn't that amazing?

647
00:44:01,972 --> 00:44:03,182
[sighs contentedly]

648
00:44:04,016 --> 00:44:05,851
[whoops] Manila. Manila.

649
00:44:10,230 --> 00:44:11,231
[sighs]

650
00:44:11,523 --> 00:44:13,984
Now, it's time to contact Jaguar.

651
00:44:20,949 --> 00:44:23,661
-Looks like she's lost.
-So, wanna nab her?

652
00:44:23,744 --> 00:44:25,245
-Yeah, let's follow her.
-Sure.

653
00:44:29,333 --> 00:44:30,459
[Anna] Please give them some sandwiches.

654
00:44:30,542 --> 00:44:31,418
Hello, everyone!

655
00:44:31,502 --> 00:44:32,544
[Anna] I'm sure they're all hungry.

656
00:44:32,628 --> 00:44:35,464
Let's take a little break.

657
00:44:35,547 --> 00:44:37,174
I'm sure you're all pretty hungry.

658
00:44:37,257 --> 00:44:39,468
-[applause]
-Dig in.

659
00:44:39,968 --> 00:44:41,178
[Danny] Thank you, Governor.

660
00:44:41,261 --> 00:44:43,055
-[Loring] Pandoy!
-[Fernan] Come on, Pandoy.

661
00:44:43,138 --> 00:44:43,889
[Camia] Pandoy is very hungry.

662
00:44:43,972 --> 00:44:45,349
Come back if you want some more!

663
00:44:45,432 --> 00:44:46,684
-[Loring] You're still running.
-[Diego] Here.

664
00:44:46,767 --> 00:44:48,769
-You might hurt yourself.
-Here, Uncle. Some juice.

665
00:44:48,852 --> 00:44:50,020
Thank you.

666
00:44:50,104 --> 00:44:51,146
[Jepoy] Diego.

667
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:54,024
As early as now,
I want to congratulate you.

668
00:44:54,108 --> 00:44:56,193
You really deserve to be governor.

669
00:45:01,323 --> 00:45:02,366
Thanks.

670
00:45:07,371 --> 00:45:09,164
Well then, in a couple of hours,

671
00:45:09,248 --> 00:45:14,795
we'll find out whether all our efforts
will bring us the bacon.

672
00:45:15,337 --> 00:45:17,172
Don't worry.
I'm sure victory will be yours.

673
00:45:18,215 --> 00:45:19,550
All right then, excuse me.

674
00:45:21,009 --> 00:45:22,761
[Julio] Please, enjoy the meal.

675
00:45:28,434 --> 00:45:31,228
-Congratulations!
-Oh. Thank you. Thank you.

676
00:45:32,312 --> 00:45:33,397
Thank you. Thank you.

677
00:45:33,480 --> 00:45:35,357
-I can't wait for the results.
-[laughs]

678
00:45:35,441 --> 00:45:36,692
Congressman.

679
00:45:36,775 --> 00:45:39,653
-Hi, Miss Aguas.
-I mean, Governor.

680
00:45:39,736 --> 00:45:41,530
-[chuckles]
-Congrats!

681
00:45:42,030 --> 00:45:43,782
Thank you, thank you, Miss Aguas.

682
00:45:43,866 --> 00:45:48,579
You know, you've been
a big help to this campaign.

683
00:45:48,662 --> 00:45:51,415
You're one of the people
behind this success.

684
00:45:51,498 --> 00:45:55,294
Even in the early days
of Arnaldo's campaign.

685
00:45:56,086 --> 00:45:57,171
You are one of the reasons

686
00:45:57,254 --> 00:46:01,300
why the Ardientes
will continue to rule this land.

687
00:46:02,551 --> 00:46:05,262
This land that was named after our family.

688
00:46:09,141 --> 00:46:11,226
-Congressman.
-Yes?

689
00:46:11,310 --> 00:46:13,520
Diego's in the lead in most
of the neighborhoods.

690
00:46:15,147 --> 00:46:16,607
Don't panic, dear.

691
00:46:17,316 --> 00:46:18,734
This fight isn't over.

692
00:46:19,485 --> 00:46:21,570
Let's all just celebrate, okay?

693
00:46:21,653 --> 00:46:23,739
-Yes.
-Go on, don't worry.

694
00:46:23,822 --> 00:46:26,283
[tense music playing]

695
00:46:40,422 --> 00:46:42,007
[reporter] <i>Diego has a lead</i>

696
00:46:42,090 --> 00:46:44,593
<i>over Congressman Julio Ardiente</i>
<i>in the votes.</i>

697
00:46:47,137 --> 00:46:48,180
[people exclaim]

698
00:46:48,263 --> 00:46:51,433
<i>We won't lose hope. You will win, Diego.</i>

699
00:46:51,517 --> 00:46:53,852
[Emilia] <i>An Ardiente never loses.</i>

700
00:46:53,936 --> 00:46:57,272
<i>I will always be an Ardiente,</i>
<i>and no one can take that away from me.</i>

701
00:46:57,356 --> 00:47:00,734
<i>I will rise up and destroy you all.</i>

702
00:47:00,817 --> 00:47:04,863
[Julio] <i>My grandson. Victory is yours.</i>

703
00:47:05,989 --> 00:47:08,909
<i>Tell me who should pay.</i>

704
00:47:11,411 --> 00:47:14,373
[theme music playing]
